# ExamFlex App — Core Standards

Student-facing NEET/JEE prep web app (Next.js App Router). Mobile-first, also tablet and desktop.

## Non-negotiables

- **TypeScript strict**: no `any`, no untyped escapes. Prefer explicit types, `unknown` + narrowing, and discriminated unions.
- **Tests with every change**: new/changed behavior ships with unit and/or component tests. Aim for **full coverage** of touched code; do not merge untested logic.
- **Separation of concerns**: UI in `components/`, domain types in `types/`, pure helpers in `lib/`, hooks in `hooks/`. Keep pages thin.
- **Responsive by default**: design mobile first (`base` → `sm` → `md` → `lg`). Touch targets ≥ 44px. Verify layouts at ~390px, ~768px, and ≥1024px.
- **Accessible**: semantic HTML, labels, keyboard support, sensible contrast.
- **ExamFlex naming**: use ExamFlex / `examflex` in new code and copy. Do not invent alternate product names.

## Stack conventions

- Next.js App Router + React 19 + Tailwind 4 + Lucide icons
- Colocate tests as `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` next to the source
- Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` only when needed
